# One-command build orchestration

Implement `tools/build/auto.py` as an optional one-command user flow that runs
dependency bootstrap, preflight, architecture selection, and build in order
while persisting each decision JSON so repeated or interrupted runs use
explicit evidence instead of hidden process state.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Run `dependencies.py`, `check.py`, `arch.py`, and `run.py` in declared
  order without duplicating their domain logic.
- [ ] Persist all decisions and validation evidence beneath `.cache/build/data/`
  with versioned schemas.
- [ ] Revalidate saved evidence on resume and never trust stale paths, hashes,
  or tool versions implicitly.
- [ ] Keep ordinary user interaction limited to actionable errors and the
  architecture checklist.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency is required beyond the declared repository and
platform prerequisites.

